Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:36:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/35] Port to upstream v1.19.0: version fallback and examples

The NAS series applied to v1.19.0 with three hand-resolved conflicts:
- settings.c: upstream took dirty bits 140 (JS8_SUBMODE) and 141 (RXA_AMBW),
  so DIRTY_RELAY moves from 140 to 142 (check_dirty_bits: no collisions);
- ui.c: upstream took drawer section 50 (JS8SUB), so Radio source is 51 and
  N_DRAWER_SECTIONS is 52;
- CMakeLists.txt: upstream's configure-on-commit block and the -NAS version
  block are both kept.
This commit points the version fallback and the examples at v1.19.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
---
 CMakeLists.txt            | 6 +++---
 README.md                 | 2 +-
 main/idf_component.yml    | 2 +-
 tools/nas-relay/README.md | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 2da15b80..9298857a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -43,14 +43,14 @@ foreach(_gitdep ".git/HEAD" ".git/index" ".git/refs/tags" ".git/packed-refs")
 endforeach()
 
 # Network-radio build: report the release it is based on plus "-NAS"
-# (e.g. v1.18.0-NAS) instead of git describe's v1.18.0-3-g<hash>-dirty, which
+# (e.g. v1.19.0-NAS) instead of git describe's v1.19.0-3-g<hash>-dirty, which
 # is too long for the UI. The update check compares only the numbers before the
-# first '-', so v1.18.0-NAS counts as v1.18.0.
+# first '-', so v1.19.0-NAS counts as v1.19.0.
 execute_process(COMMAND git describe --tags --abbrev=0
                 WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}
                 OUTPUT_VARIABLE QMX_BASE_TAG OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE ERROR_QUIET)
 if(NOT QMX_BASE_TAG)
-    set(QMX_BASE_TAG "v1.18.0")
+    set(QMX_BASE_TAG "v1.19.0")
 endif()
 set(PROJECT_VER "${QMX_BASE_TAG}-NAS")
 
